{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"balsamy-eloquent-iggypops","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The `Verified` gate's `pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.11)` cell hangs after ~99% of the suite and is cancelled at the 60-minute job timeout\n\n## Symptom\n\nThe cell prints progress normally for ~10 minutes, reaches `[ 99%]` with **zero** `F`/`E`\nmarkers, and then emits nothing at all until GitHub kills it:\n\n    2026-08-07T17:04:16.9396830Z ....................................... [ 99%]\n    2026-08-07T17:55:12.0420609Z ##[error]The operation was canceled.\n\n`timeout-minutes: 60` is set on the `test` job in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`.\nThe CI bot reads the cancellation as a failure and votes `Verified -1` + `Code-Review -1`,\nso an otherwise-green change cannot land.\n\n## Not change-specific\n\nSeen on at least two unrelated changes on 2026-08-07:\n\n* change 1505 (`9fb3`), three consecutive runs — 31194624887, 31199714760, 31206898501 —\n  including one run **after** a rebase onto `origin/main` @ 9532650f24.\n* run 31208164115, a different change, same signature: `[ 99%]` then\n  `The operation was canceled.`\n\nThe other matrix cells (ubuntu py3.12, ubuntu py3.13, macos py3.13) complete the same\nselection in 11-21 minutes on those same runs, so it is specific to the ubuntu/py3.11 cell.\n\nCounting the progress dots on run 31199714760's cell: 11160 of ~11215 tests had reported\nbefore the silence, so roughly the last ~55 tests are where it stalls. It is a hang in the\ntest tail, not in coverage combining or teardown after the run.\n\n## Does not reproduce locally\n\nOn macOS with the CI-faithful configuration — `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra\nreviewbot --extra ui --python 3.11`, then `REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 pytest -m \"not\nintegration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q -p no:cacheprovider --durations=25\n--cov=rebar` — the suite finishes in 15:00 with 11196 passed, 19 skipped, exit 0. So the\ntrigger involves the Linux runner (4 vCPU, `fcntl.flock`-backed store locking) rather than\nthe interpreter version alone.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nEvery change in flight can be blocked by a red `Verified` that reflects no real defect, and\nthe only workaround is to keep posting `recheck` until a run happens to get through. That is\nthe same class of problem as a gating advisory failure: the gate stops discriminating.\n\n## Suggested first moves\n\n- Add `-v` (or `--timeout` via `pytest-timeout`) to the ubuntu cells so the hanging test\n  names itself instead of being invisible behind `-q` dots.\n- Suspect first the store's write-lock paths (`fcntl.flock` + `mkdir`) and any test that\n  shells out to `rebar` as a subprocess, since a blocked lock acquire is the shape that\n  produces exactly this silence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the hanging test (or the blocking call) is named, with a CI log line or a local\n      reproduction showing it stalled\n- [ ] the ubuntu py3.11 cell completes within the 60-minute job timeout on three\n      consecutive Verified runs\n- [ ] whatever makes the hang diagnosable (a per-test timeout, `-v`, or a faulthandler\n      dump) is committed, so a recurrence names itself instead of going silent","id":"89d5-61da-b621-47f8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI: the ubuntu-latest/py3.11 pytest cell hangs at 99% and is killed by the 60-minute job timeout"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786129724511504001,"uuid":"8c0722cd-7f8f-4384-ae3b-630b26f649cb"}